{
  "version": 1,
  "canonicalRoot": "tools/schema-sync/typespec",
  "handMirrorDocs": "Hand mirror entries verify that hand-maintained native/TS schema copies still carry every field the generated canon defines (field name + optionality). Each entry may be a bare path string (checked against every generated *Doc interface in the domain) or an object { path, interfaces?, language?, knownDrift? }. `interfaces` pins which generated interfaces the mirror must carry; omit it to require all of them. `knownDrift` grandfathers the pre-existing divergences enumerated by check-hand-mirror.mjs (each entry is `Interface.field` for a missing field or `Interface.field#opt` for an optionality mismatch); the checker FAILS when live drift exceeds the listed set, so new drift is caught while the strangler migration burns the list down. legacy.ts is registered as a `tsHandMirror` so its dual-defined doc types are field-checked against the generated canon.",
